viewcore reads a type's pointer map from GCData. Go reaches the map of a type
with more than internal/abi.MaxPtrmaskBytes*8 pointer words through one more
pointer (internal/abi.TFlagGCMaskOnDemand): GCData points at a slot in the
binary's BSS, and the runtime stores the map's address there the first time it
needs it. Unpatched, the reader reads the slot as the map and walks past the end
of the binary's memory: "address ... is not mapped in the core file".

This follows the slot at all three places GCData is read. A slot still nil, or
holding runtime.inProgress, has no map yet, and every word is treated as a
possible pointer.

Applied by scripts/install-viewcore.sh to the commit scripts/lib/tool-versions.sh
pins. scripts/core-walk-check.sh walks the same core with the newest upstream
reader, unpatched, and fails the night that reads it too: then this file goes.

